@c ===================================================================
@node CMacs API
@chapter CMacs API

@cindex CMacs API
@cindex libcmacs-api
@cindex init.c

The CMacs API is a shared C library (@file{libcmacs-api.so}) that
provides a high-level interface for interacting with the CMacs editor
from C code.  It is used by both the @command{cmacsgi} bacon builtin
and by Crispy C scripts (including @file{init.c}).

@section Transport Backends

The API supports three transport backends, auto-detected in order:

@table @strong
@item DIRECT
In-process function calls via a registered dispatch table.  Used by
Crispy scripts, which are compiled to @file{.so} files and loaded into
the Emacs process via @code{g_module_open()}.  Zero IPC overhead.

The dispatch table is a struct of function pointers registered by
@code{cmacs-crispy.c} before executing scripts:

@example
typedef struct @{
    gchar    *(*eval)(const gchar *expression, GError **error);
    void      (*find_file)(const gchar *path);
    void      (*message)(const gchar *text);
    gboolean  (*gi_require)(const gchar *ns, const gchar *ver,
                            GError **error);
    gchar    *(*gi_call)(const gchar *ns, const gchar *func,
                         const gchar *const *args, gint n_args,
                         GError **error);
    gchar   **(*gi_list_functions)(const gchar *ns);
@} CmacsApiDirectDispatch;
@end example

@item FD
Length-prefixed JSON over a Unix socketpair (@env{CMACS_IPC_FD}).
Used by the Bacon child process.

Messages are framed as: @code{[4 bytes: uint32 BE length][N bytes: JSON]}.
Maximum message size is 16@tie{}MiB.  Timeout is 30 seconds.

Request format:

@example
@{"id": 1, "method": "Eval", "params": @{"expression": "(+ 40 2)"@}@}
@end example

@noindent
Method parameter mappings:

@multitable @columnfractions .25 .75
@headitem Method @tab JSON params
@item @code{Eval} @tab @code{@{"expression": "..."@}}
@item @code{FindFile} @tab @code{@{"path": "..."@}}
@item @code{Message} @tab @code{@{"text": "..."@}}
@item @code{GiRequire} @tab @code{@{"namespace": "...", "version": "..."@}}
@item @code{GiCall}
@tab @code{@{"namespace": "...", "function": "...", "args": [...]@}}
@item @code{GiListFunctions} @tab @code{@{"namespace": "..."@}}
@end multitable

@noindent
Response: @code{@{"result": "42"@}} on success,
@code{@{"error": "message"@}} on error.

@item D-Bus
GDBusProxy to @code{org.cmacs.Editor1} (@env{CMACS_DBUS_NAME}).
Used by external tools.  Connects on the session bus with object
path @code{/org/cmacs/Editor}.  GVariant params pass through
directly (no JSON translation).
@end table

@section High-Level C API

Include @code{<cmacs-api.h>} and link with @code{-lcmacs-api}.
All functions return 0 on success unless noted otherwise.

@table @code
@item CmacsApi *cmacs_api_new (GError **error)
Create a handle (auto-detects transport).  Returns @code{NULL} on
failure.

@item void cmacs_api_free (CmacsApi *api)
Free the handle and all associated resources.

@item gint cmacs_set (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *var, const gchar *value)
Set an Emacs variable.  Numbers and @code{t}/@code{nil} pass through
as Lisp values; everything else becomes a quoted string.
Generates: @code{(setq VAR VALUE)}.

@item gint cmacs_get (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *var, gchar **out)
Get an Emacs variable value.  On success, stores the printed Lisp
representation in @code{*out} (caller must @code{g_free}).

@item gint cmacs_theme (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *name)
Load a color theme.  Generates: @code{(load-theme 'NAME t)}.

@item gint cmacs_font (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *family, gint size)
Set the default font and size.  Pass @code{size <= 0} to leave size
unchanged.  Point sizes less than 100 are converted to 1/10 point
units (14 becomes 140).  Generates:
@code{(set-face-attribute 'default nil :family "FAMILY" :height SIZE)}.

@item gint cmacs_mode (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *name)
Enable a mode.  Appends @code{-mode} if not already present.
Generates: @code{(NAME-mode 1)}.

@item gint cmacs_eval (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *elisp)
Evaluate arbitrary elisp.

@item gint cmacs_open (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *path)
Open a file via the @code{FindFile} transport method.

@item gint cmacs_message (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *text)
Display a message in the echo area.

@item gint cmacs_pkg_install (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *name)
Install a package via @code{package.el}.  Automatically refreshes
package contents if the package is not already installed.

@item gint cmacs_pkg_remove (CmacsApi *api, const gchar *name)
Remove a package.
@end table

@section Low-Level Transport API

@table @code
@item CmacsApiTransport *cmacs_api_transport_new (GError **error)
Auto-detect and create a transport.  Returns @code{NULL} on failure.

@item void cmacs_api_transport_free (CmacsApiTransport *t)
Free the transport.  Does not close the fd (caller owns it).

@item GVariant *cmacs_api_transport_call (CmacsApiTransport *t, const gchar *method, GVariant *params, GError **error)
Call a method with GVariant parameters.  Returns the result GVariant
(caller must @code{g_variant_unref}), or @code{NULL} on error.
@end table

@noindent
Supported method signatures:

@multitable @columnfractions .25 .25 .25 .25
@headitem Method @tab Params @tab Returns @tab Description
@item @code{Eval} @tab @code{(s)} @tab @code{(s)} @tab Evaluate elisp
@item @code{FindFile} @tab @code{(s)} @tab (none)
@tab Open file
@item @code{Message} @tab @code{(s)} @tab (none)
@tab Echo area msg
@item @code{GiRequire} @tab @code{(ss)} @tab @code{(b)}
@tab Load GI namespace
@item @code{GiCall} @tab @code{(ssas)} @tab @code{(s)}
@tab Call GI function
@item @code{GiListFunctions} @tab @code{(s)} @tab @code{(as)}
@tab List GI functions
@end multitable

@section Eval Helpers

@table @code
@item gint cmacs_api_eval_print (CmacsApiTransport *t, const gchar *elisp)
Evaluate elisp via transport, print result to stdout.

@item gint cmacs_api_eval_quiet (CmacsApiTransport *t, const gchar *elisp)
Evaluate elisp, suppress output.

@item gchar *cmacs_api_eval_get_string (CmacsApiTransport *t, const gchar *elisp)
Evaluate elisp, return result as string (caller must @code{g_free}).
@end table

@section String Utilities

@table @code
@item gchar *cmacs_api_lisp_escape (const gchar *s)
Escape a C string for embedding in a Lisp string literal.  Escapes
@code{\} and @code{"}.  Does not add outer quotes.  Caller must
@code{g_free}.

@item gchar *cmacs_api_lisp_quote (const gchar *s)
Quote a value for the Lisp reader: numbers, @code{t}/@code{nil},
quoted strings, and s-expressions pass through; bare words become
quoted string literals.  Caller must @code{g_free}.
@end table

@section Dispatch Table Types

Used by @command{cmacsgi} command implementations to organize
subcommands into groups.

@table @code
@item CmacsApiHandler
@code{typedef gint (*CmacsApiHandler)(CmacsApiTransport *transport, gint argc, gchar **argv);}

@item CmacsApiSubcmd
Struct: @code{@{ const gchar *name; CmacsApiHandler handler; const gchar *usage; const gchar *help; @}}.

@item gint cmacs_api_dispatch_group (group_name, table, transport, argc, argv, depth)
Dispatch @code{argv[depth]} against a NULL-terminated subcommand table.
Handles @code{--help}/@code{-h}.

@item void cmacs_api_print_group_help (group_name, table)
Print formatted help listing for a subcommand group.
@end table

@section Example: init.c

@example
/* ~/.config/cmacs/init.c */
#include <cmacs-api.h>

int main(int argc, char **argv)
@{
    CmacsApi *api = cmacs_api_new(NULL);
    if (!api) return 1;

    /* Appearance */
    cmacs_theme(api, "modus-vivendi");
    cmacs_font(api, "Iosevka", 14);

    /* Settings */
    cmacs_set(api, "inhibit-startup-screen", "t");
    cmacs_set(api, "ring-bell-function", "ignore");
    cmacs_set(api, "scroll-conservatively", "101");

    /* Modes */
    cmacs_mode(api, "electric-pair");
    cmacs_mode(api, "global-display-line-numbers");
    cmacs_mode(api, "column-number");

    /* Packages */
    cmacs_pkg_install(api, "magit");
    cmacs_pkg_install(api, "which-key");

    /* Keybindings */
    cmacs_eval(api, "(global-set-key (kbd \"C-x g\") 'magit-status)");

    /* Open a file */
    cmacs_open(api, "~/Documents/notes/todo.org");

    cmacs_message(api, "C config loaded!");
    cmacs_api_free(api);
    return 0;
@}
@end example

