@node Podomation Bacon Builtin
@section Bacon Builtin

The @code{pod} builtin is available in the bacon shell.  It connects
to CMacs via the API transport layer (FD/D-Bus/direct).

@multitable @columnfractions .35 .65
@headitem Command @tab Description
@item @code{pod start} @tab Start the engine
@item @code{pod stop} @tab Stop the engine
@item @code{pod status} @tab Show running state
@item @code{pod modules} @tab List loaded modules
@item @code{pod pods} @tab List active pods
@item @code{pod stats} @tab Show engine statistics
@item @code{pod eval DSL_TEXT} @tab Evaluate DSL text
@item @code{pod load FILE} @tab Load a @file{.pod} file
@item @code{pod repl} @tab Enter interactive REPL
@item @code{pod --help} @tab Show all commands
@item @code{pod help COMMAND} @tab Help for a command
@end multitable

@subsection Example Session

@example
$ pod start
t
$ pod modules
timer
cron
http
...
cmacs
gowl
$ pod eval "pod t = timer->new(5000); \
    t->on_tick => print->string(\"tick\");"
t
$ pod pods
t	healthy
$ pod stats
events-dispatched: 3
handlers-called: 3
handlers-failed: 0
pipe-chains-executed: 3
$ pod repl
Podomation REPL (type :quit to exit)
podomation> :modules
LOADED MODULES:
  cmacs   [source+handler]  CMacs Emacs integration
  ...
podomation> pod x = timer->new(1000); \
    x->on_tick => print->string("hello");
podomation> :pods
ACTIVE PODS:
  t        healthy
  x        healthy
podomation> :quit
$ pod stop
t
@end example

@node Podomation GI Access
@section GObject Introspection Access

If the Podomation-1.0 typelib is built:

@example
make -C deps/podomation typelib
@end example

Then the full podomation API is accessible from Elisp via GI:

@lisp
(gi-require "Podomation" "1.0")

;; Access engine stats directly
(gi-call "Podomation" "engine_stats_new")

;; Access module manager
(let ((engine (cmacs-podomation-get-engine)))
  (gi-call "Podomation" "engine_get_module_manager" engine))
@end lisp

This provides access to the full GObject API beyond what the DEFUNs
expose.

@node Podomation Examples
@section Examples

@subsection Auto-start with Pod Files

@lisp
;; In init.el
(setq cmacs-podomation-auto-start t)
(setq cmacs-podomation-pod-files
      '("~/.config/cmacs/hooks.pod"
        "~/.config/cmacs/timers.pod"))
@end lisp

@subsection Notify on Build Failure

@example
pod c = cmacs->new();
c->on_compile_finish
    where event->exit_code != "0"
    => gotify->send("Build failed in @{event->buffer_name@}");
@end example

@subsection Focus Tracking with Logging

@example
pod g = gowl->new();
g->on_focus_change
    => log->write_info("Focus: @{event->app_id@} - @{event->title@}");
@end example

@subsection Auto-save Reminder via Timer

@example
pod t = timer->new(300000);
t->on_tick => cmacs->eval("(message \"Consider saving your work\")");
@end example

@subsection HTTP Health Monitor

@example
pod h = http->new();
pod t = timer->new(60000);
t->on_tick => h->get("https://api.example.com/health");
h->on_response
    where event->status_code != "200"
    => slack->send("#alerts", "API unhealthy: @{event->status_code@}");
@end example

@subsection Pipe Chain: Transform and Log

@example
pod c = cmacs->new();
c->on_buffer_save
    => transform->uppercase("@{event->file_name@}")
     | log->write_info("SAVED: @{pipe->value@}");
@end example

@subsection Conditional: Different Actions by Mode

@example
pod c = cmacs->new();
if c->on_buffer_save where event->major_mode == "python-mode" @{
    c->on_buffer_save
        => shell->exec("ruff check @{event->file_name@}");
@} else @{
    c->on_buffer_save
        => print->string("saved @{event->file_name@}");
@}
@end example

@subsection Regex: Parse Log Lines

@example
pod j = journal->new();
j->on_entry
    where event->message =~
        "(?P<level>ERROR|WARN) (?P<service>\\w+): (?P<msg>.*)"
    => gotify->send(
        "@{rematch->level@} in @{rematch->service@}: @{rematch->msg@}");
@end example

@subsection Client Auto-tiling Rule

@example
pod g = gowl->new();
g->on_client_map
    where event->app_id == "firefox"
    => gowl->view_tags("2");
@end example

