@node CMacs Audio
@chapter CMacs Audio: GStreamer Capture and Playback

@cindex cmacs-audio
@cindex audio
@cindex pipewire
@cindex pulseaudio

@quotation
This chapter mirrors @file{doc_org/cmacs/cmacs-audio.org}; that file
is the canonical interactive reference.  Updates land in both.
@end quotation

@section Overview

cmacs-audio is the audio counterpart to @code{cmacs-video}.  It wires
two GStreamer pipeline shapes through the same cmacs @code{GMainContext}:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Capture}: @code{pipewiresrc} (or @code{pulsesrc} fallback)
@code{! audioconvert ! audioresample ! capsfilter(audio/x-raw,format=S16LE,channels=1,rate=16000) ! appsink}.
The default 16 kHz/mono/S16LE caps are whisper.cpp-ready; PCM drained
via @code{cmacs-audio-read-pcm} can be passed straight to
@code{cmacs-whisper-transcribe-pcm} without resampling.
@item
@strong{Playback}: either @code{playbin3 uri=URI} (file/HTTP) or
@code{appsrc ! audioconvert ! audioresample ! volume ! autoaudiosink}
(for streaming PCM, the path used by Piper TTS output).
@end itemize

Inline @code{#+BEGIN_AUDIO :src "file.wav"} org blocks render a cairo
waveform SVG overlay (see @code{cmacs-audio-waveform-svg}); the org
overlay is an inline image rather than a per-frame cairo blit, so the
pgtk paint hook is only used for standalone-anchored streams.

@section Quick Start

@example
;; Capture 5 seconds to a WAV
(cmacs-audio-record-to-file "/tmp/note.wav" 5)

;; Play a file
(cmacs-audio-play-file "~/music/sample.opus")

;; Inline #+BEGIN_AUDIO block
;;   #+BEGIN_AUDIO :src "note.wav" :width 800 :height 100
;;   Voice note
;;   #+END_AUDIO

;; Bound under C-c v
C-c v r        cmacs-audio-record-to-file
C-c v R        cmacs-audio-finish-recording
C-c v p        cmacs-audio-play-file
C-c v x        cmacs-audio-stop-all
@end example

@section Defcustoms

@table @code
@item cmacs-audio-capture-source
Default capture source: @code{auto} (pipewiresrc with pulsesrc
fallback), @code{pipewire}, @code{pulse}, @code{coreaudio}, or
@code{test}.

@item cmacs-audio-default-rate
Sample rate in Hz (default 16000).

@item cmacs-audio-default-channels
1 (mono) or 2 (stereo); default 1.

@item cmacs-audio-default-device
Optional PipeWire/Pulse device hint.  Nil = system default.

@item cmacs-audio-output-dir
Where recordings + sidecar WAVs land
(default @file{~/Documents/notes/03_resources/cmacs-audio/}).

@item cmacs-audio-mode-line-indicator
Show a per-stream count in the mode-line when audio is live.
@end table

@section Build Requirements

System packages (Fedora):

@example
sudo dnf install \
  pipewire-devel pipewire-libs pulseaudio-libs-devel \
  cmake gcc-c++ pipx espeak-ng \
  gstreamer1-plugins-good
@end example

@code{gcc-c++} is required for vendored @code{deps/whisper.cpp}
(C++).  @code{pipx} + @code{espeak-ng} are runtime deps for Piper.
The @code{install-deps} script handles all of this per-distro.

@section Composition

@itemize
@item @code{cmacs-whisper}: 16k mono S16LE caps mean drained PCM is
whisper-ready.  Live dictation: @code{C-c v d} (cmacs-whisper-dictate).
@item @code{cmacs-piper}: PCM emitted by Piper is fed into
@code{cmacs-audio--playback-open-pcm-1} for live output.
@item @code{podomation}: fires @code{on_transcription_ready} and
@code{on_voice_command} events; DSL rules can respond with the
@code{speak} handler (which calls @code{cmacs-piper-speak-async}).
@item @code{libreclaw}: @code{M-x cmacs-libreclaw-send-voice-message}
records, transcribes via whisper if built, and sends the transcript
into the active bridge room.
@end itemize

@c ===================================================================
@node CMacs Whisper
@chapter CMacs Whisper: Offline Speech-to-Text

@cindex cmacs-whisper
@cindex whisper.cpp
@cindex speech to text
@cindex STT

@quotation
This chapter mirrors @file{doc_org/cmacs/cmacs-whisper.org}; that file
is the canonical interactive reference.
@end quotation

@section Overview

cmacs-whisper integrates whisper.cpp for offline speech-to-text.
Models are loaded on first reference into a thread-safe path → context
cache; inference runs on a GThread worker so the Emacs main thread
never blocks.  Completion is delivered back to the main thread via
@code{g_main_context_invoke (cmacs_glib_get_context())}, where the
registered Lisp callback fires.

@section Model Search Path

Model files are resolved through @code{cmacs-whisper-models-search-path},
which by default looks in two locations:

@enumerate
@item
@file{~/.local/share/cmacs/whisper-models/} — user-writable dir where
@kbd{M-x cmacs-whisper-download-model} writes new models.
@item
@file{/usr/share/cmacs/whisper-models/} — system dir populated by
container image builds.  The default English model
(@code{ggml-base.en.bin}, 142 MB) is bundled here by
@code{./build-container}.
@end enumerate

User-installed models take precedence (search-path walks in order).

@subsection Overriding the bundled model

Pass build-time args to @code{./build-container} to swap the
language/size shipped in the image:

@example
WHISPER_MODEL_NAME=ggml-small.en.bin \
WHISPER_MODEL_URL=https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp/resolve/main/ggml-small.en.bin \
  ./build-container
@end example

The default English-base model is a good real-time choice on CPU;
swap to @code{small} or @code{medium} for higher accuracy at the
cost of latency and memory.

@subsection Build path

When neither a system @code{whisper.pc} nor an installed library is
present, configure falls back to the vendored
@code{deps/whisper.cpp/} submodule.  The CMake build is invoked with:

@example
cmake -B build -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DGGML_OPENMP=OFF \
      -DWHISPER_BUILD_TESTS=OFF -DWHISPER_BUILD_EXAMPLES=OFF \
      -DCMAKE_C_STANDARD=11 -DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD=17 \
      -DCMAKE_C_STANDARD_REQUIRED=ON -DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED=ON
@end example

The C/CXX standard flags are a workaround for a CMake 4.x feature-
detection table that doesn't yet know about GCC 16+; setting the
standards explicitly makes @code{target_compile_features} a no-op.

cmacs links the resulting static libraries in this order:

@example
deps/whisper.cpp/build/src/libwhisper.a
deps/whisper.cpp/build/ggml/src/libggml.a
deps/whisper.cpp/build/ggml/src/libggml-cpu.a
deps/whisper.cpp/build/ggml/src/libggml-base.a
-lm -lstdc++ -lpthread
@end example

Requires @code{gcc-c++} (Fedora) or @code{g++} (Debian) on the build
host — installed by @code{install-deps}.

@section Quick Start

@example
M-x cmacs-whisper-download-model RET ggml-base.en.bin RET
(cmacs-whisper-transcribe-file
  (cmacs-whisper-model-path)
  "/tmp/note.wav")
;; => ((:text . "...full text...")
;;     (:segments . (((:start . 0) (:end . 1200) (:text . "..."))
;;                   ...)))
@end example

@section Live Dictation (cmacs-whisper-dictate)

@kbd{M-x cmacs-whisper-dictate} (bound to @kbd{C-c v d}) toggles a
buffer-local dictation mode.  Speak into the microphone; whisper's
own end-of-utterance VAD detects pauses and emits each finalised
segment, which is inserted at point with @code{undo-boundary} between
segments so each utterance is one undo unit.

Voice commands intercepted before insertion (configured via
@code{cmacs-whisper-dictate-command-words}):

@table @code
@item "new line"     -> newline
@item "new paragraph" -> two newlines
@item "period"       -> ?.
@item "question mark" -> ??
@item "delete word"  -> backward-kill-word
@item "undo"         -> undo
@end table

@section MCP Tool

The @code{transcribe} MCP tool (registered when both
@code{--with-cmacs-mcp} and @code{--with-cmacs-whisper} are built)
accepts @code{audio_path} + optional @code{language} and returns the
transcript text.  Companion read-only tool: @code{list_whisper_models}.

@section Defcustoms

@table @code
@item cmacs-whisper-models-directory
User-writable models dir (default
@file{~/.local/share/cmacs/whisper-models/}).

@item cmacs-whisper-system-models-directory
System models dir populated by image builds (default
@file{/usr/share/cmacs/whisper-models/}).

@item cmacs-whisper-models-search-path
Ordered list of dirs searched for model files; default
@code{(cmacs-whisper-models-directory cmacs-whisper-system-models-directory)}.

@item cmacs-whisper-default-model
Default model filename (e.g. @code{ggml-base.en.bin}).

@item cmacs-whisper-language
ISO 2-letter language code (default @code{"en"}).

@item cmacs-whisper-download-base-url
Upstream model mirror; default
@code{https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp/resolve/main/}.

@item cmacs-whisper-dictate-window-seconds
Sliding window length for live dictation (default 3.0 s).

@item cmacs-whisper-dictate-auto-punctuate
Capitalise + space inserted segments (default t).

@item cmacs-whisper-dictate-command-words
