@node Cintrospect
@chapter Cintrospect: Runtime C Self-Introspection

@cindex cintrospect
@cindex DWARF
@cindex libdw
@cindex runtime C introspection

@quotation
This chapter mirrors @file{doc_org/cmacs/cintrospect.org}; that file
is the primary interactive reference and contains the full follow-along
tutorial.  Read it for examples and architecture details; this chapter
gives the reference summary.
@end quotation

CMacs already lets you redefine Elisp at runtime.  The @code{cintrospect}
subsystem closes the @emph{read} half of that gap for the C layer:
parse the running binary's DWARF debug info via libdw (elfutils) and
expose structured access from Lisp and from MCP.  Phase 2 will add
runtime C compilation via libgccjit.  The companion
@code{cpatch} subsystem (next chapter) closes the @emph{write} half.

Enable with @option{--with-cmacs-cintrospect} (default on).  Adds
elfutils-devel + libdebuginfod to the build deps and appends
@code{-fno-omit-frame-pointer -fasynchronous-unwind-tables -gdwarf-5}
to CFLAGS so DWARF queries and stack walks work reliably.

@section Lisp DEFUNs

@table @code
@item cmacs-c-list KIND &optional GLOB LIMIT
List entities; KIND is @code{symbol}, @code{defun}, or @code{object}.

@item cmacs-c-symbol-info NAME
Return plist of @code{:symbol-name :kind :addr :size :object :file :line}.

@item cmacs-c-type-info NAME
Return plist of @code{:kind :size :align :fields}; @code{:fields} is a
list of per-field plists with @code{:symbol-name :addr :size :type-name :bit-size}.

@item cmacs-c-function-source NAME
Return @code{(file . line)} or @code{nil}.

@item cmacs-c-addr-to-source ADDR
Return @code{(file line function)} list or @code{nil}.

@item cmacs-c-source-to-addr FILE LINE
Inverse: return integer or @code{nil}.

@item cmacs-c-list-objects
List loaded ELF objects with @code{:has-dwarf} flag.

@item cmacs-c-list-defuns &optional GLOB LIMIT
List every Lisp-callable C primitive.

@item cmacs-c-defun-info SYM
Return plist for the DEFUN named SYM (lookup via obarray).

@item cmacs-c-stack-trace &optional DEPTH
List of plists for the current C stack.

@item cmacs-c-compile SOURCE FUNC-NAME &optional EXPECTED-SIG
@itemx cmacs-c-call HANDLE &rest ARGS
@itemx cmacs-c-handle-info HANDLE
@itemx cmacs-c-handle-dispose HANDLE
JIT (Phase 2) DEFUNs.  In Phase 1 these signal
@code{cmacs-cintrospect-not-implemented}.
@end table

@section Interactive buffers

@table @code
@item M-x cmacs-c-introspect
Top-level dashboard with live counts and links to sub-browsers.

@item M-x cmacs-c-list-symbols
@code{*cmacs-c-symbols*} tabulated-list-mode browser.

@item M-x cmacs-c-show-type RET NAME RET
@code{*cmacs-c-type: NAME*} struct/union/enum layout viewer.

@item M-x cmacs-c-show-defun RET SYM RET
@code{*cmacs-c-defun: SYM*} per-DEFUN detail.

@item M-x cmacs-c-show-stack
@code{*cmacs-c-stack*} live C stack with file:line.

@item M-x cmacs-c-list-defuns-buffer
@itemx M-x cmacs-c-list-objects-buffer
DEFUN registry / loaded-ELF-objects browsers.
@end table

@section File reference

@table @file
@item cmacs/cintrospect/cmacs-cintrospect.c
Top-level subsystem entry; all Lisp DEFUNs.

@item cmacs/cintrospect/cmacs-cintrospect-dwarf.c
libdw/libdwfl wrapper: symbol lookup, addr↔source, recursive type
DIE walking.  All entry points hold a coarse mutex (libdw is not
thread-safe).

@item cmacs/cintrospect/cmacs-cintrospect-defun.c
Walks @code{Vobarray} via @code{DOOBARRAY} for SUBRP entries; exposes
@code{cmacs_cintrospect_defun_swap_fn} primitive used by cpatch.

@item cmacs/cintrospect/cmacs-cintrospect-jit.c
@itemx cmacs/cintrospect/cmacs-cintrospect-marshal.c
Phase-2 stubs: persistent gcc_jit_context + DWARF-driven
Lisp@dmn{}C blob marshaller.

@item lisp/cmacs/cmacs-cintrospect.el
High-level Lisp API + autoloads + @code{tabulated-list-mode}
browsers + @code{with-help-window} detail buffers.
@end table

@section Bacon Integration

The full DEFUN surface --- @code{cmacs-c-list},
@code{cmacs-c-symbol-info}, @code{cmacs-c-type-info},
@code{cmacs-c-function-source}, @code{cmacs-c-addr-to-source},
@code{cmacs-c-list-objects}, @code{cmacs-c-list-defuns},
@code{cmacs-c-defun-info}, @code{cmacs-c-stack-trace},
@code{cmacs-c-symbol-value}, @code{cmacs-c-symbol-set-value},
@code{cmacs-c-compile}, @code{cmacs-c-call},
@code{cmacs-c-handle-info}, @code{cmacs-c-handle-dispose} --- is
reachable from the bacon shell via the @code{cmacsgi c} subcommand
group.  See @ref{cmacsgi Builtin}, section @samp{C Runtime
Introspection Commands}, for full subcommand reference, examples,
and the JIT compile/call walkthrough.

